    "hld": {
      "title": "High-Level Design",
      "mermaid": "flowchart TD\n  subgraph Runtime\n    main[\"Boot and bare-metal loop<br/>Core/Src/main.c: HAL_Init, app_start, app_process\"]\n    app[\"Motor command application<br/>firmware/app/app.c: app_start, app_process\"]\n    lifecycle[\"Motor lifecycle control<br/>firmware/services/motor_lifecycle/motor_lifecycle.c\"]\n    waveform[\"Three-phase waveform generation<br/>firmware/modules/motor_waveform/motor_wavef…\"]\n    board[\"STM32 motor-board adapter<br/>firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c\"]\n  end\n  subgraph MotorHardware\n    tim1[\"PWM timer<br/>TIM1, 20 kHz\"]\n    phase_u[\"Motor phase U output<br/>PA8, TIM1 channel 1\"]\n    phase_v[\"Motor phase V output<br/>PA9, TIM1 channel 2\"]\n    phase_w[\"Motor phase W output<br/>PA10, TIM1 channel 3\"]\n    standby[\"Driver standby control<br/>PC9\"]\n    fault[\"Enable and fault input<br/>PB12\"]\n    driver[\"X-NUCLEO-IHM16M1 STSPIN830 driver<br/>x_nucleo_ihm16m1_drive_motor\"]\n  end\n  subgraph SerialInterface\n    usart2[\"Command UART<br/>USART2, TX PA2, RX PA3\"]\n    console[\"Console and UART logging<br/>HAL_UART_Transmit, printf\"]\n  end\n  led[\"Status LED<br/>PA5\"]\n\n  main -->|app_start and app_process| app\n  main -->|HAL_GPIO_TogglePin| led\n  app -->|motor_lifecycle_process| lifecycle\n  lifecycle -->|motor_waveform_step| waveform\n  app -->|motor_board_* interface| board\n  app -->|uart_if_read_byte and uart_if_write| usart2\n  app -->|LOGI and LOGE| console\n  main -->|uart_if_initialize and probe| usart2\n  usart2 -->|USART2 serial data| console\n  board -->|HAL_TIM_PWM_Start and compare updates| tim1\n  tim1 -->|TIM1 CH1 PWM| phase_u\n  tim1 -->|TIM1 CH2 PWM| phase_v\n  tim1 -->|TIM1 CH3 PWM| phase_w\n  board -->|x_nucleo_ihm16m1_set_standby| standby\n  fault -->|HAL_GPIO_ReadPin| board\n  board -->|x_nucleo_ihm16m1 driver callbacks| driver\n  driver -->|three PWM inputs| phase_u\n  driver -->|three PWM inputs| phase_v\n  driver -->|three PWM inputs| phase_w\n  driver -->|STBY GPIO| standby\n  driver -->|EN/FAULT GPIO| fault",
      "authored_by_model": true,
      "node_notes": {
        "standby": "PC9 drives the STSPIN830 standby control through the X-NUCLEO-IHM16M1 GPIO_STBY callback. The binding is APP_MOTOR_STBY_GPIO_PORT and APP_MOTOR_STBY_GPIO_PIN in app_config.h, with writes implemented by HAL_GPIO_WritePin.",
        "phase_v": "PA9 is the motor phase V PWM output and is configured as GPIO_AF6_TIM1. app_config.h names it APP_MOTOR_PHASE_V_GPIO_PORT and the board adapter maps it to TIM1 channel 2.",
        "phase_u": "PA8 is the motor phase U PWM output and is configured as GPIO_AF6_TIM1. app_config.h names it APP_MOTOR_PHASE_U_GPIO_PORT and firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c assigns it to TIM1 channel 1.",
        "driver": "The X-NUCLEO-IHM16M1 driver exposes motor drive, standby, fault, and PWM callback operations for the STSPIN830 board. firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c initializes it with three PWM inputs and callback functions implemented over TIM1 and GPIO.",
        "tim1": "TIM1 generates the three PWM channels used for the motor phases at the configured 20 kHz motor PWM frequency. stm32_motor_board.c configures TIM1 and uses HAL_TIM_PWM_Start and compare-register updates for channels 1 through 3.",
        "console": "This is the real serial sink for startup, status, command responses, and LOG macros. uart_if_write reaches HAL_UART_Transmit in uart_stm32.c, while logger.h maps LOGI and LOGE to printf output routed by the platform.",
        "usart2": "USART2 provides the command and response transport with transmit on PA2 and receive on PA3 at 115200 baud. firmware/platforms/stm32/uart_stm32.c configures GPIO_AF7_USART2, uses interrupt reception, and transmits through HAL_UART_Transmit.",
        "led": "PA5 is the NUCLEO-G431RB user status LED and is toggled from the main loop. app_config.h identifies APP_LED_GPIO_PORT and APP_LED_GPIO_PIN, and Core/Src/main.c calls HAL_GPIO_TogglePin.",
        "lifecycle": "This module tracks stopped, starting, running, and fault motor states and ramps electrical frequency. firmware/services/motor_lifecycle/motor_lifecycle.c calls motor_waveform_step during motor_lifecycle_process.",
        "board": "This STM32 adapter binds the portable motor-board interface to HAL GPIO, TIM1 PWM, and the X-NUCLEO-IHM16M1 driver. firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c implements motor_board_prepare, motor_board_apply_pwm, motor_board_read_fault, and motor_board_shutdown.",
        "waveform": "This module converts electrical angle, frequency, amplitude, and direction into three U/V/W duty values. firmware/modules/motor_waveform/motor_waveform.c implements motor_waveform_step with three phase-shifted sine calculations.",
        "phase_w": "PA10 is the motor phase W PWM output and is configured as GPIO_AF6_TIM1. app_config.h names it APP_MOTOR_PHASE_W_GPIO_PORT and the board adapter maps it to TIM1 channel 3.",
        "fault": "PB12 is the enable/fault input read by the motor-board adapter with an internal pull-up. stm32_motor_board.c uses HAL_GPIO_ReadPin on APP_MOTOR_EN_FAULT_GPIO_PORT and APP_MOTOR_EN_FAULT_GPIO_PIN and converts the active-low level using APP_MOTOR_FAULT_ACTIVE_LEVEL.",
        "main": "This is the STM32 entry path that initializes HAL, probes USART2, calls app_start, and repeatedly calls app_process. The evidence is Core/Src/main.c, including HAL_GPIO_TogglePin on the PA5 LED and HAL_Delay using APP_LED_PERIOD_MS.",
        "app": "This application owns UART command processing, motor lifecycle calls, status reporting, and logging. firmware/app/app.c provides app_start, app_process, process_uart, and dispatch_command, and sends responses through uart_if_write."
      }
    },
    "lld": {
      "title": "Low-Level Design (Firmware Workflow)",
      "mermaid": "flowchart TD\n  subgraph BareMetalLoop\n    boot[\"Start board and application<br/>Core/Src/main.c: HAL_Init, uart_if_initialize, …\"]\n    init[\"Prepare motor board and initialize command state<br/>firmware/app/app.c: app_st…\"]\n    poll[\"Read and assemble incoming UART command lines<br/>firmware/app/app.c: process_u…\"]\n    parse{\"Complete line and valid command — firmware/app/app.c: process_uart\"}\n    dispatch[\"Dispatch command and send response<br/>firmware/app/app.c: dispatch_command\"]\n    tick{\"Elapsed time at least 1 ms — firmware/app/app.c: app_process\"}\n    faultcheck{\"Fault read failed or fault active — firmware/app/app.c: app_process\"}\n    lifecycle_step[\"Advance lifecycle and generate U, V, W duties<br/>firmware/services/motor_lifec…\"]\n    pwm[\"Apply three-phase PWM duties<br/>firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c: …\"]\n    shutdown[\"Force zero duty, stop PWM, and enter standby<br/>firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32…\"]\n    led_toggle[\"Toggle status LED<br/>Core/Src/main.c: HAL_GPIO_TogglePin\"]\n    delay[\"Wait before the next main-loop iteration<br/>Core/Src/main.c: HAL_Delay, APP_LE…\"]\n  end\n\n  boot -->  init\n  init -->  poll\n  poll -->  parse\n  parse -->|yes| dispatch\n  parse -->|no or incomplete| tick\n  dispatch -->  tick\n  tick -->|yes| faultcheck\n  tick -->|no| led_toggle\n  faultcheck -->|yes| shutdown\n  faultcheck -->|no| lifecycle_step\n  lifecycle_step -->|true| pwm\n  lifecycle_step -->|false| shutdown\n  pwm -->  led_toggle\n  shutdown -->  led_toggle\n  led_toggle -->  delay\n  delay -->|200 ms| poll",
      "authored_by_model": true,
      "node_notes": {
        "dispatch": "dispatch_command handles STATUS, direction, frequency, duty, start, and stop commands and writes acknowledgements or errors. firmware/app/app.c also performs the start fault check before enabling the motor.",
        "shutdown": "Shutdown forces all three duties to zero, stops TIM1 PWM, and places the driver in standby. These operations are implemented by motor_board_shutdown in firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c.",
        "led_toggle": "The status LED is toggled once per main-loop iteration independently of the 1 ms motor-control gate. Core/Src/main.c calls HAL_GPIO_TogglePin on the configured PA5 LED.",
        "delay": "The main loop waits with HAL_Delay using APP_LED_PERIOD_MS, configured as 200 ms. After the delay, execution returns to UART polling and the next application iteration.",
        "boot": "This step represents the actual reset-to-application path rather than Cube clock boilerplate. Core/Src/main.c performs HAL initialization and UART setup before entering app_start and the bare-metal loop.",
        "lifecycle_step": "This step ramps frequency, advances the electrical angle, generates three phase duties, and changes the lifecycle to running when processing succeeds. motor_lifecycle_process in firmware/services/motor_lifecycle/motor_lifecycle.c returns false when the lifecycle is not starting or running.",
        "parse": "A completed CR/LF line is accepted only when command_transport_line_push reports completion and command_parser_parse succeeds. The branch is implemented in process_uart in firmware/app/app.c and uses the command parser in firmware/modules/command_parser/command_parser.c.",
        "faultcheck": "The application reads the motor driver fault input before producing a new waveform. firmware/app/app.c treats either a failed motor_board_read_fault call or an active fault as a fault path.",
        "init": "app_start prepares the motor board, initializes UART command transport and motor lifecycle state, then shuts the motor down initially. The evidence is firmware/app/app.c, including motor_board_prepare, command_transport_line_initialize, motor_lifecycle_initialize, and motor_board_shutdown.",
        "tick": "The motor control update is gated by APP_MOTOR_CONTROL_PERIOD_MS, which is 1 ms. app_process computes elapsed time from osal_uptime_ms and enters the control path only when the interval has elapsed.",
        "pwm": "The generated duty_u, duty_v, and duty_w values are passed to the motor board adapter. firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c forwards them to x_nucleo_ihm16m1_drive_motor, which updates TIM1 channel compares through the PWM callback.",
        "poll": "process_uart drains bytes supplied by the USART2 interrupt-backed receive queue and pushes them into the command-line buffer. firmware/app/app.c calls uart_if_read_byte and command_transport_line_push for each available byte."
      }
    },
    "sequence": {
      "title": "Sequence Diagram",
      "mermaid": "sequenceDiagram\n  participant Boot as main.c boot\n  participant App as app_process\n  participant UART as USART2 UART\n  participant Parser as command parser\n  participant Lifecycle as motor lifecycle\n  participant Board as motor board adapter\n  participant TIM1 as TIM1 PWM\n  participant Motor as STSPIN830 motor driver\n  participant LED as PA5 status LED\n  participant Console as UART console\n\n  Boot->>UART: uart_if_initialize\n  UART-->>Console: uart init ok\n  Boot->>Console: main uart probe\n  Boot->>App: app_start\n  App->>Board: motor_board_prepare\n  Board->>TIM1: configure PWM channels 1, 2, and 3\n  Board->>Motor: x_nucleo_ihm16m1_init\n  App->>Board: motor_board_shutdown\n  Board->>Motor: set standby and zero PWM\n  App->>Console: app start and firmware started\n\n  loop main while loop with 200 ms LED delay\n    App->>UART: uart_if_read_byte\n    alt complete valid command\n      App->>Parser: command_parser_parse\n      Parser-->>App: command kind and parameters\n      App->>Lifecycle: update direction, frequency, duty, start, or stop\n      App->>UART: uart_if_write response\n    else invalid or incomplete input\n      App-->>App: retain line state or send invalid response\n    end\n\n    opt elapsed time reaches 1 ms\n      App->>Board: motor_board_read_fault\n      Board->>Motor: x_nucleo_ihm16m1_read_fault\n      alt fault active or read failure\n        App->>Lifecycle: motor_lifecycle_fault\n        App->>Board: motor_board_shutdown\n        Board->>TIM1: stop PWM and clear duties\n        Board->>Motor: enter standby\n      else no fault\n        App->>Lifecycle: motor_lifecycle_process\n        Lifecycle-->>App: U, V, and W duty outputs\n        App->>Board: motor_board_apply_pwm\n        Board->>Motor: x_nucleo_ihm16m1_drive_motor\n        Motor->>TIM1: update channels 1, 2, and 3\n      end\n    end\n    Boot->>LED: HAL_GPIO_TogglePin PA5\n  end",
